{"created": "2024-02-22T23:10:13.600525+00:00", "modified": "2024-02-22T23:10:13.857650+00:00", "id": 10694880, "conceptrecid": "10694879", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10694880", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.10694879", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10694880", "metadata": {"title": "Multi-Session longitudinal MI training dataset", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10694880", "publication_date": "2024-02-22", "description": "<p>This dataset contains data from 18 subjects recorded over 6 sessions conducted on different days. The details of data acquisition protocol are mentioned in this paper \"<a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/pnasnexus/advance-article/doi/10.1093/pnasnexus/pgae076/7609232\">Transfer learning promotes acquisition of individual BCI skills</a>\" . Detailed dataset descriptions in terms of triggers and basic helper functions are provided in this <a href=\"https://github.com/neurosatya/TransLearning\">repository</a> . If you end up using this dataset for benchmarking BCI algorithms please cite,</p>\n<p>@article{kumar2024transfer,<br>&nbsp; title={Transfer learning promotes acquisition of individual BCI skills},<br>&nbsp; author={Kumar, Satyam and Alawieh, Hussein and Racz, Frigyes Samuel and Fakhreddine, Rawan and Mill{\\'a}n, Jos{\\'e} del R},<br>&nbsp; journal={PNAS Nexus},<br>&nbsp; pages={pgae076},<br>&nbsp; year={2024},<br>&nbsp; publisher={Oxford University Press}<br>}</p>\n<p>For more information on the dataset, please contact the authors.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Satyam Kumar", "affiliation": "UT Austin", "orcid": "0000-0003-4817-1768"}, {"name": "Hussein Alawieh", "affiliation": "UT Austin", "orcid": "0000-0002-2888-4958"}, {"name": "Racz, Frigyes Samuel", "affiliation": "The University of Texas at Austin", "orcid": "0000-0001-9077-498X"}, {"name": "Rawan Fakhreddine", "affiliation": "UT Austin", "orcid": "0000-0002-6012-4019"}, {"name": "Jos\u00e9 del R. Mill\u00e1n", "affiliation": "UT Austin", "orcid": "0000-0001-581